; fas9_special_dimensions.scr - facit of step 9.17 (F9.20 ARC_DIMENSION and LARGE_RADIAL_DIMENSION, and the DIMASSOC part of F9.8).
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_special_dimensions.scr
; starts AutoCAD 2025's core on acad.dwt (a new empty drawing). Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (see fas9_example.scr).
; An empty line is Enter; a command with a point to pick is given the coordinates of the pick, which the core resolves against the
; objects (ZOOM Extents first: a pick far from the view is not found). DIMASSOC 2 makes the dimensions associative: a point that is
; an object snap (_end) or an object that is picked has its DIMASSOC point reference; a bare coordinate gives none ("Non-associative
; dimension created").
;
; What is made (model space unless said):
;   dim_special                  a triangle (three LINEs), two circles and two arcs; DIMLINEAR (picked object), DIMALIGNED (endpoints),
;                                DIMANGULAR (two lines), DIMRADIUS, DIMDIAMETER, two DIMORDINATE, DIMARC (arc, then a partial one),
;                                DIMJOGGED (circle with centre override, jog and text positions; arc)
;   dim_special <change>         one change per file, cumulative: a circle moved, a vertex stretched, an arc scaled, the text of an arc
;                                dimension moved (DIMTEDIT), one dimension disassociated (DIMDISASSOCIATE) and one reassociated
;                                (DIMREASSOCIATE), a referenced circle erased
;   dim_special_paper            the same kinds in paper space (Layout1)
;   dim_special_block            DIMARC and DIMJOGGED inside a block, the block inserted
;
; Not made here (plan 9.17, "Ej testat", F9.8/F9.20): an intersection object snap (_int) or a subentity marker on a 3D solid (no solid
; dimensions in the core's DIM commands), a reference into an xref (DIMASSOC's external strings 301/302: the core has no second drawing
; here), the text of an arc or jogged dimension edited with DIMEDIT New (the in-place text editor), grips for the jog or the arc
; symbol (no window).
